Article 2 For the purposes of these Regulations, "Olympic symbols" refer to:
(1) the Olympic five-ring pattern symbol, Olympic flag, Olympic motto, Olympic emblem, and Olympic anthem of the International Olympic Committee;
(2) the exclusive names such as Olympic, Olympia, Olympic Games, and their abbreviations;
(3) the name, emblem, and symbol of the Chinese Olympic Committee;
(4) the name, emblem, and symbol of the institution applying to host the Olympic Games within the territory of China;
(5) the names and their abbreviations, mascots, anthems, torch designs, slogans, symbols such as "host city name + year of hosting" of the Olympic Games held within the territory of China, as well as the names and emblems of their organizing bodies;
(6) other symbols related to the Olympic Games held within the territory of China as specified in the Olympic Charter and the relevant host city contract for the Olympic Games.

Article 5 For the purposes of these Regulations, "use for commercial purposes" means the use of Olympic symbols for profit-making purposes in the following manners:
(1) applying the Olympic symbols to goods, goods packaging or containers, and commercial transaction documents;
(2) applying the Olympic symbols to service items;
(3) applying the Olympic symbols to advertising, commercial exhibitions, commercial performances, and other commercial activities;
(4) selling, importing, or exporting goods containing Olympic symbols;
(5) manufacturing or selling Olympic symbols;
(6) other acts of using Olympic symbols for profit-making purposes.

Article 13 With respect to acts infringing the exclusive right to Olympic symbols, the market supervision and administration department shall have the authority to investigate and handle them according to law.
When investigating and handling acts suspected of infringing the exclusive right to Olympic symbols based on obtained evidence of illegal suspicion or reports, the market supervision and administration department may exercise the following powers:
(1) inquiring of the relevant parties and investigating the circumstances related to the infringement of the exclusive right to Olympic symbols;
(2) consulting and copying contracts, invoices, account books, and other relevant materials related to the infringing activities;
(3) conducting on-site inspections of the places where the parties are suspected of engaging in activities infringing the exclusive right to Olympic symbols;
(4) inspecting articles related to the infringing activities; and sealing up or detaining articles that have evidence proving to be infringing the exclusive right to Olympic symbols.
When the market supervision and administration department exercises the powers set forth in the preceding paragraph according to law, the parties shall provide assistance and cooperation, and shall not refuse or obstruct.
